<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rafic Hariri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1944–2005</span> · Also known as Rafiq al-Hariri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rafic Hariri was a Lebanese businessman who made his fortune in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and served as prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> in 1992–1998 and 2000–2004, leading the reconstruction of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a> after the civil war. His assassination by a car bomb on 14 February 2005 set off mass protests, the Cedar Revolution, which forced Syrian troops to leave Lebanon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rafic-hariri.jpg" alt="Rafic Hariri" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Commission - Christian Lambiotte · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visit_of_Rafic_Hariri,_Lebanese_Prime_Minister,_to_the_EC_P010848002H_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
